What is Renewable Energy Certificate (REC)?
Renewable Energy Certificates (RECs) are tradable commodities that certify one megawatt-hour (MWh) of electricity generated from eligible renewable sources like solar, wind, biomass, geothermal, and hydropower. These certificates separate the environmental benefits of renewable generation from the energy itself, enabling buyers to meet regulatory compliance or voluntary sustainability targets. By purchasing RECs, organizations can offset conventional energy use and demonstrate commitment to cleaner power.
